<title>RUSSIA: Russia to offer 10.5 trln rbls in T-bills on Oct 1.</title>
<headline>Russia to offer 10.5 trln rbls in T-bills on Oct 1.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian finance ministry will offer 7.50 trillion roubles in six-month Treasury bills and 3.00 trillion roubles in a new tranche of three-month T-bills on October 16, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the six-month T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		     22054</p>
<p>    Issue volume			7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				 245 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			  Oct 16, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     June 18, 1997</p>
<p>The bill actually run for eight months, but are officially classified as six-month paper.</p>
<p>Full details of the three-month T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		     21071</p>
<p>    Issue volume			3.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)		 98 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			  Oct 16, 1996</p>
<p>    Original issue date	     Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     Jan 22, 1997</p>
<p>The issue yielded an average 69.12 percent when it was first sold.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
